Then, $\quad(h, k)=\left(\frac{x_{1}+a}{2}, \frac{y_{1}+0}{2}\right)$
\begin{aligned}
&\Rightarrow \quad h=\frac{x_{1}+a}{2} \text { and } k=\frac{y_{1}}{2} \\
&\Rightarrow \quad x_{1}=2 h-a \text { and } y_{1}=2 k
\end{aligned}

Since, $P\left(x_{1}, y_{1}\right)$ lies on parabola $y^{2}=4 a x$, then

\begin{array}{r}
(2 k)^{2}=4 a(2 h-a) \\
4 k^{2}=4 a(2 h-a) \\
k^{2}=2 a\left(h-\frac{a}{2}\right) \\
y^{2}=2 a\left(x-\frac{a}{2}\right)
\end{array}

Equation of its directrix is

\begin{aligned}
\Rightarrow \quad x-\frac{a}{2} &=\frac{-a}{2} \\
\Rightarrow \quad x &=0
\end{aligned}
